{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  GUILLO — image alt text
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Returns the alt text for a product image. One place, so the product page,
  the product cards and the cart cannot drift apart.

  Order of preference:
    1. The image's OWN alt, as set on the media in Shopify admin. Always wins.
    2. Product title plus colour, e.g. "The Luxe Chino in Black".
    3. Product title alone, when no colour can be established.

  Nothing is hardcoded here: every word comes from the product's own data.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE THING THAT MAKES THIS SNIPPET NECESSARY

  Liquid's media.alt is NEVER blank for product media. When no alt text is set
  in admin, Shopify quietly returns the PRODUCT TITLE instead. So a theme that
  does alt: media.alt looks correct in the markup while actually shipping no
  real description at all. Checked 2026-10-03: 224 of the 258 images on the 48
  active products have an empty alt in the Admin API, yet every one of them was
  already rendering the product title on the storefront.

  So an alt that is exactly equal to the product title is treated as "no alt",
  which lets the colour be added. Colour is what separates one colourway from
  another in Google Images, and it is the one fact the title never carries.
  If someone has genuinely typed the product title in as the alt text, adding
  the colour is still an improvement, so this is safe either way.
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Colour is read from custom.colour_name first (11 of 48 active products have
  it, and it is already nicely cased), then the "colour:" tag (43 of 48). No
  product currently has a Color/Colour option, so that is not consulted.

  The "#note:" convention: some PDP media carry alt text like
  "Front view #note:Model is 188cm" so sections/guillo-product.liquid can pull
  a caption out of it. Only the part before #note: describes the picture, so
  that is all that reaches the alt attribute.

  Params:
    media_alt : the raw alt string from the media (optional)
    product   : the product it belongs to (optional, used for the fallback)

  Usage:
    {%- capture img_alt -%}
      {%- render 'guillo-image-alt', media_alt: media.alt, product: product -%}
    {%- endcapture -%}
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign gia_alt = ''

  if media_alt != blank
    assign gia_alt = media_alt
    if gia_alt contains '#note:'
      assign gia_alt = gia_alt | split: '#note:' | first
    endif
    assign gia_alt = gia_alt | strip
  endif

  # Shopify's silent title fallback, see the note above. Treat it as no alt.
  if product.title != blank and gia_alt == product.title
    assign gia_alt = ''
  endif

  if gia_alt == blank and product.title != blank
    assign gia_colour = product.metafields.custom.colour_name.value | default: ''

    if gia_colour == blank
      for gia_tag in product.tags
        if gia_tag contains 'colour:'
          assign gia_colour = gia_tag | split: 'colour:' | last | strip | replace: '-', ' ' | capitalize
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    if gia_colour != blank
      assign gia_alt = product.title | append: ' in ' | append: gia_colour
    else
      assign gia_alt = product.title
    endif
  endif
-%}
{{- gia_alt -}}
